course: dictionary
lesson: 14727
title: Profoundly: going deep
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Profoundly is an adverb. It tells you how much or how deeply something happens. You can ask: how grateful? Profoundly grateful means very, very grateful, with feelings that go deep.
explain: «Maya was profoundly grateful for the warm blanket.» The word profoundly makes grateful stronger. Try the swap: «Maya was grateful for the warm blanket» still makes sense, but the word profoundly shows that she felt it very strongly.
explain: Profoundly can also describe health. «Sam is profoundly deaf» means he hears very little or nothing. This is a respectful, clear way to describe it. Some words, like profoundly, are used in special ways in certain subjects, so check the clues around them.
fact: Profoundly means very deeply or greatly.
fact: «Profoundly grateful» means very, very thankful.
fact: «Profoundly changed» means changed in a big, deep way.
fact: In health, «profoundly deaf» means hearing very little or nothing.
fact: Profoundly can also mean in a wise, deep-thinking way, as in «He spoke profoundly about life.»
exercise: «Maya was profoundly grateful for the warm blanket.» What does profoundly mean here? | *Very deeply or greatly | Quietly, in a whisper | Only just | Slowly and carefully
exercise: «Sam is profoundly deaf.» What does profoundly tell you about his hearing? | *Hearing very little or nothing | Hearing very well, even in a noisy room | Being very quiet in class | Hearing only sometimes, on a good day
exercise: «He spoke profoundly about life.» What does profoundly mean here? | Very loudly | *In a wise, deep-thinking way | Very quickly, in a hurry | Without any clothes
test: «The story profoundly changed Priya.» Which word tells how much the story changed her? | Changed | Story | *Profoundly | Priya
test: Ben was ___ affected by the news. Which word fits best? | Quickly | Often | *Profoundly | Slowly
exam: «The child was profoundly different after the holiday.» Which meaning fits best? | Quietly sad | Only a little bit different | Asleep for hours | *Very greatly different
